{
  "about": "A range of a text file (gamma/highlights.py text_position, docs/dev/api.md \"The highlight shape\"): its columns are 0-based code points of the decoded line, and its quote, prefix and suffix are cut from the lines joined with \\n. lines holds the decoded file's lines; span a range as given (line and end 1-based, end inclusive, end_col exclusive); utf16 the same columns in UTF-16 code units (clamped to their lines), as CodeMirror counts them; trimmed, when present, the span as it is stored: each column at most its line's length, an end at column 0 of a later line (or after line breaks alone) moved back to the end of the line before, null when nothing is left; quote the text of the stored span, at most quote_max code points and never ending in a line break, prefix and suffix the context code points just before it and just after it. A start at its line's end (or before line breaks alone) moves on to the start of the next line. spans: a stored position and the span its readers take from it (highlights.text_span, blockModel.textSpan), null for a malformed one. max_text_bytes: the largest file the viewer shows whole and a run places ranges in (textLoad.MAX_TEXT_BYTES, text_anchors.TEXT_RELOCATE_MAX_BYTES). backend/tests/test_shared_fixtures.py reads it through highlights.span_text and clamp_span, frontend/tests/textAnchors.test.mjs through textAnchors.contextOf, toCodePoints and toCodeUnits.",
